From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen6@xiaomi.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:50:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: export rpmsg_unregister_endpoint()

A device being torn down has to unregister its endpoints without
sending NS_DESTROY, which can no longer reach the remote.

Signed-off-by: Bowen Wang <wangbowen6@xiaomi.com>
---
 lib/rpmsg/rpmsg.c          |  2 +-
 lib/rpmsg/rpmsg_internal.h | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg.c open-amp/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg.c
index 0c82897..76521fd 100644
--- a/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg.c
+++ open-amp/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg.c
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ int rpmsg_set_priority(struct rpmsg_endpoint *ept, uint8_t priority)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static void rpmsg_unregister_endpoint(struct rpmsg_endpoint *ept)
+void rpmsg_unregister_endpoint(struct rpmsg_endpoint *ept)
 {
 	struct rpmsg_device *rdev = ept->rdev;
 
diff --git a/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg_internal.h open-amp/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg_internal.h
index 686ef07..854e8a3 100644
--- a/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg_internal.h
+++ open-amp/lib/rpmsg/rpmsg_internal.h
@@ -144,6 +144,18 @@ void rpmsg_register_endpoint(struct rpmsg_device *rdev,
 			     rpmsg_ept_cb cb,
 			     rpmsg_ns_unbind_cb ns_unbind_cb, void *priv);
 
+/**
+ * @internal
+ *
+ * @brief Unregister an endpoint without notifying the remote
+ *
+ * For a device that is going away, where the remote can no longer be told.
+ * Clears ept->rdev, so a later rpmsg_destroy_ept() on it is a no-op.
+ *
+ * @param ept	pointer to a registered rpmsg endpoint
+ */
+void rpmsg_unregister_endpoint(struct rpmsg_endpoint *ept);
+
 static inline struct rpmsg_endpoint *
 rpmsg_get_ept_from_addr(struct rpmsg_device *rdev, uint32_t addr)
 {
-- 
2.34.1

